In-Reply-To: <68bbfdd41001250548t6a0f863w994e2cea79b4f0b5@mail.gmail.com>
References: <68bbfdd41001250548t6a0f863w994e2cea79b4f0b5@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <e71a39ea1001250940o2b17316uea48c32815d8bdb8@mail.gmail.com>

If you use the oligo package, everything is already in place:

http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/data/annotation/html/pd.raex.1.0.st.v1.html

with oligo, you'll be able to use RMA and get summaries at the
probeset and gene levels:

library(oligo)
cels = list.celfiles()
theData = read.celfiles(cels)
probesetSumm = rma(theData, target="probeset")
geneCoreSumm = rma(theData, target="core")
geneExtendedSumm = rma(theData, target="extended")
geneFullSumm = rma(theData, target="full")


cheers,
b

