Dear list,

Here is a job advertisement posted on behalf of Owen Solberg and Prescott
Woodruff. If you are interested, please contact
Prescott.woodruff at ucsf.edu.

Post-Doctoral Position in Applied Bioinformatics
University of California, San Francisco

The Woodruff Laboratory of the UCSF Airway Clinical Research Center is a 
rapidly growing laboratory that combines human studies of Asthma and 
Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) with genome-wide gene 
expression microarray analyses. To take optimal advantage of a large 
existing tissue bank and ongoing clinical studies, we are pleased to 
announce an opening for a Post-Doctoral Position in Applied
Bioinformatics.

Desirable experience: Computational biology with strong background in 
genomics and systems biology.

Position: The position is funded by a grant from the NIH/NHLBI (R01 HL- 
095372, Molecular Phenotyping of Asthma). The project has applied genomic 
analyses to airway samples from patients with asthma to distinguish 
Th2-driven and non-Th2-driven sub-phenotypes of asthma that have distinct 
clinical, pathological and treatment-related characteristics. Ongoing 
analyses are aimed at identifying gene expression markers in lung tissue 
samples of inflammation and remodeling in these two sub-groups of asthma 
and identifying whole blood gene expression markers of these clinical 
phenotypes. Additional studies have been initiated using miRNA arrays and 
applying similar approaches to study COPD and Interstitial Lung Diseases. 
